@using Orbit.Core.Text
@using Orbit.Web.Services

@* A description, with the web addresses in it pressable instead of copied out by hand.

   Every run is added as content, never as markup: LinksInText hands back text and addresses, and
   Blazor escapes both. That is what makes this safe to point at a description somebody else wrote and
   shared - see LinksInText for why only http and https ever become an href.

   A new tab, because a description is read in the middle of doing something: following a link out of a
   half-written list is the one thing nobody meant to do. rel="noopener noreferrer" with it, so the page
   opened cannot reach back through window.opener and is not told where it was linked from.

   A link to somebody else's map is the exception, and opens Orbit's own instead (MapPageLink, asked for
   on 2026-09-19): the place is pinned there with its address, a way to start an event or a list at it,
   a way to be taken there, and the original link still one press away. In this tab, because it is a
   page of Orbit's and not somewhere else. *@
@foreach (var run in LinksInText.Split(Text))
{
    @if (run.Url is { } url)
    {
        @if (MapPageLink.For(url) is { } onOrbitsMap)
        {
            <a class="map-link" href="@onOrbitsMap" title="@(T["Open it on Orbit's map"])">@run.Text</a>
        }
        else
        {
            <a href="@url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@run.Text</a>
        }
    }
    else
    {
        @run.Text
    }
}

@code {
    [Inject] private Translations T { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>What was written. Empty or null draws nothing at all, not an empty element.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Text { get; set; }
}
